# J96 GPU: wide PMGR clock snapshot (gpu-pmgr-clock-wide), 2026-11-16 ~06:45 GMT, fresh j96-boot.
# Kernel 7.3.0-rc1-j96-firstboot+. Module gpu/probe/apple-j96-gpubridge.ko sha256 3b9f9aa6...59cbb1,
# loaded after unbinding the built-in apple-j96-gpuprobe; text console in front. Completed, result=0;
# the iPad stayed up. All 352 words (pmgr +0xN000..+0xN03c for N = 0..5, +0x1c000..+0x1c3fc) are
# readable with GFX off; most were read for the first time. No RGX access.
#
# Findings:
# - The six clock pages share one layout. +0xc..+0x14 and +0x20/+0x24 are the same constants on all
#   six (081c8385 01ac0418 02187000 / 14790c38 000004b6). They differ only in +0x0 (config), +0x4
#   (status), +0x8, +0x18 and +0x1c:
#     running (pages 1, 4): +0 bit31 set, +4 = 0x40000000, +0x18 = 0x04000040, +0x1c = 0xbc/0xbd040000
#     idle    (pages 0,2,3): +0 = 0x1010, +4 = 0x80000001, +0x18 = 0x00000001, +0x1c = 0x0c040000
#     page 5:                +0 = 0x1010, +4 = 0x00000000, +0x18 = 0x00000001, +0x1c = 0x04040000, +8 bit24 set
#   Page 5 is in a third state, unlike both the running and the idle pages.
# - GPC 0 -> 1 reaches page 5: right after the poll, page 5 +0x1c gains bit 27 (04040000 -> 0c040000,
#   the idle pages' value) and pmgr +0x1c200 goes 80000000 -> 80110100. At +1 s, +0x1c200 is still
#   80110100 but page 5 +0x1c is back to 04040000. Page 5 +0 and +4 never change: the PLL is not
#   configured and never reports the 0x40000000 status the running pages (and J81 iPadOS) show.
# - Page 1 +0x1c bit 26 dropped once right after ps_gfx on and was back by the next snapshot
#   (probably a live status bit).
# - +0x1c000..: only the slots already known (8 entries, 365/450/550/600 MHz and their halves);
#   +0x1c100..+0x1c1fc, +0x1c204.., +0x1c304.. are all zero. No other control word in the area.
#
